 "about": [
  "Guernésiais is Guernsey's own Norman language, close kin to Jèrriais in Jersey.",
  "The 2001 census found 1,327 fluent speakers, most of them over 64.",
  "When children were evacuated in 1940, ahead of the Occupation, many never learnt it, and it has been fragile since."
